# External-agent credentials for the MCP `ask` tool.
#
# Install as /opt/laplace/secrets/agents.env (mode 0640, owned by the run user).
# bootstrap-host.sh already provisions /opt/laplace/secrets as the secrets drop;
# this file joins lichess.env and stripe.env there.
#
# WHY A FILE AND NOT JUST THE ENVIRONMENT. laplace-mcp is not a systemd service —
# an agent client spawns it over stdio and usually cannot inject environment
# variables into a child it launches from a JSON config. Laplace.Agents reads the
# process environment FIRST and falls back to this file through the same
# LaplaceInstall.TryReadConfig reader the API service uses for Stripe and
# Lichess, so a client-launched server finds the credentials the host has.
#
# Only the variables you actually use need to be present. The `agents` MCP tool
# reports, per provider, which variable it looked for and whether it resolved —
# it never returns a value.

# OPENAI_API_KEY=
# ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=
# XAI_API_KEY=
# GEMINI_API_KEY=
# OPENROUTER_API_KEY=
# GROQ_API_KEY=
# DEEPSEEK_API_KEY=
# MISTRAL_API_KEY=

# Local / self-hosted runtimes need a key only if the server enforces one.
# OLLAMA_API_KEY=
# LAPLACE_AGENT_API_KEY=

# Route used when `ask` names no model. An alias from agents.json, a
# 'provider/model' pair, or a vendor-branded model id. Outranks the config
# file's own "default".
# LAPLACE_AGENT_DEFAULT=house

# Explicit config path; otherwise the search is /opt/laplace/app/agents.json,
# then <repo>/config/agents.json, then ~/.config/laplace/agents.json.
# LAPLACE_AGENTS_CONFIG=/opt/laplace/app/agents.json
